  - graph theory
  - Python
  - C#
abstract: >-
  DTree is a minimal library for single-rooted directed trees whose
  structure is encoded by two linear projections, Q1 and Q2. Node u
  reaches node v if and only if u strictly precedes v in both projections.
  The reference implementation (Python) supports edge insertion, deletion,
  subtree moves (cut_n_paste), and path-based queries; a C# prototype is
  included.
